A mutable character set must not inherit an immutable one's init.

WHAT WAS WRONG. -[NSCharacterSet init] hands back a set made with
CFCharacterSetCreateWithCharactersInRange, which is IMMUTABLE. NSMutableCharacterSet defined no
init of its own, so it inherited that one, and every alloc init mutable character set in the whole
process was immutable. Every mutator on __NSCFCharacterSet is gated on __CFCharacterSetIsMutable,
so addCharactersInRange:, addCharactersInString: and the rest silently did NOTHING and the set
stayed empty for as long as it lived. No error, no exception, no log line.

MEASURED BEFORE AND AFTER with tests/foundation/probe_charset_membership.m, which asks exactly what
iTerm2 asks. Before, 6 of 10 assertions failed: every character added was reported absent, the copy
was empty, and the inverted set contained everything. After, 10 of 10 pass. The two controls, a
character never added and that same character in the inverted set, pass in BOTH runs, so the set
did not simply become everything.

WHAT IT COST, which is how it was found. -[VT100Grid numberOfNonEmptyLinesIncludingWhitespaceAsEmpty:]
builds an NSMutableCharacterSet of the cell codes that count as empty, by addCharactersInRange: for
0, 2 and 4 and addCharactersInString: for the rest, then scans the grid against it. With an empty
set NO cell is ever empty, so numberOfLinesUsed returned the FULL grid height, 44 where 4 lines held
text. Shrinking the window from 44 rows to 38 therefore archived six rows of real output into
scrollback to preserve content that was not there, the document stayed taller than the clip, and a
terminal bottom aligns its document, so iTerm2 blanked its own screen on every height reduction.

    before   window 1256x600   numberOfLinesUsed 44   scrollback 6   terminal BLANK
    after    window 1256x600   numberOfLinesUsed 4    scrollback 0   terminal INTACT, LOOKED AT
Survives a second shrink to 1256x560 as well.

THE REACH IS MUCH WIDER THAN ONE TERMINAL. A mutable character set is how applications build
tokenisers, trimming sets and escaping sets, and every one of them has been silently empty in this
port. iTerm2 is simply the first application that made the failure visible.

Task #247.

--- a/NSCharacterSet.m
+++ b/NSCharacterSet.m
@@ -416,6 +416,17 @@
     NSRequestConcreteImplementation();
 }
 
+/* A MUTABLE SET MUST NOT INHERIT AN IMMUTABLE ONE'S init. NSCharacterSet init hands back a
+ * CFCharacterSet created with CFCharacterSetCreateWithCharactersInRange, which is IMMUTABLE, and
+ * with no init here NSMutableCharacterSet inherited it. Every mutator on __NSCFCharacterSet is
+ * gated on __CFCharacterSetIsMutable, so addCharactersInRange: and friends silently did nothing
+ * and the set stayed empty for the life of the process. Task #247. */
+- (id)init
+{
+    [self release];
+    return (id)CFCharacterSetCreateMutable(kCFAllocatorDefault);
+}
+
 - (BOOL)isMutable
 {
     return YES;
